{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792268803,"nonce":"6foUoHZlCryBsWelpIG5YBauOvk=","title":"A typed heap census: live objects and bytes per hl_type","message":"Requested by the ChimpMonk session (their git-bug eb19594): an idle editor holds 56-69 MB live on the GC heap, about 80-285 KB per layout node, and nothing names what is heavy. hl_gc_dump_memory writes per-block live lines without types, and hl.Gc.getLiveObjects answers -1.\n\nWhat is wanted: at a major collection on demand (a Gc call; ChimpMonk's probe already runs hl.Gc.major() twice and reads stats after each stage) and at exit under ASH_GC_CENSUS=1: live count and live bytes per hl_type name, sorted by bytes, top 40 or so; noptr/hl.Bytes blocks bucketed by size; per-collection lines not needed.\n\nWhy it is not a heap walk (std/src/gc.rs, hlp_gc_get_live_objects): the Immix heap marks 128-byte lines, small objects are bump-packed 16 bytes apart inside a line, only multi-line allocations record a start (alloc_sizes), and no allocation records its type. A census therefore has to be inferred.\n\nDesign to try: after the mark that hlp_gc_dump_memory already does (no sweep), scan the marked lines of pointerful blocks at 16-byte granularity for a first word that is a known hl_type pointer, and size the object from the type: HOBJ and HSTRUCT from the runtime object's size, varray from header plus count times the element size, vdynamic boxes and closures from their fixed sizes. Known types come from a registry filled where an object runtime is created, since compiled code bumps the TLAB without calling the allocator. The census is an estimate: an object field holding a type pointer is counted as an object (rare; only HTYPE values), and an object of a type without a runtime is invisible. Noptr blocks: live bytes at line granularity from the marks, plus the multi-line allocations bucketed by their recorded sizes. The result goes into the ASHMEM1 dump text (so hl.Gc.dumpMemory(path) is the on-demand call, no new Haxe API) and to stderr at exit.\n\nAlso asked: function names for findex in the sampler's output (ASH_PROFILE=sample lists interpreted functions as findex/Fun_NNNN).","files":null}]}